.TH GPS_TOF 3 "2026-11-05" "gps-tof 0.6.0" "Library Functions"
.SH NAME
gps_tof \- Python API for geodetic time-of-flight calculations
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
from gps_tof.model import Problem, Site, Baseline, OpeningAngle, BeamAxis, TimingShift, Settings
from gps_tof.calc import compute_all, compute_baseline, compute_opening_angle, compute_face, axis_frame, point_vs_axis, direction_vs_axis, chord, final_stage, site_point
from gps_tof.report import render
from gps_tof.geodesy import geodetic_to_ecef, ecef_to_geodetic, enu_basis, enu_to_ecef_offset
from gps_tof.fermilab_site import fscs_to_geodetic, geodetic_to_fscs
from gps_tof.angles import parse_angle, dms
from gps_tof import nmea
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.SS Model (gps_tof.model)
.TP
.B Site(name, lat, lon, height_m, datum="ellipsoid", geoid_separation_m=None, offset_enu_m=(0,0,0), id="", fscs_xyz_ft=None, axis_position=None, ...)
A surveyed point and the displacement to its physics endpoint.  \fBSite.from_dict\fR accepts
the configuration-file keys (angles as strings).  \fBh_ellipsoidal\fR, \fBlat_rad\fR,
\fBlon_rad\fR, \fBcable_delay_s\fR are derived properties; \fBreplace(**changes)\fR returns a
modified copy (used for sensitivities).
.TP
.B Baseline(source, target, label="", axis_to="")
Two site ids and an optional reference-axis site.
.TP
.B BeamAxis(origin, through, label="")
The global reference line (\fBProblem.beam_axis\fR); \fBfrom_dict\fR accepts {from, to, label}.
.TP
.B OpeningAngle(vertex, a, b, label="", axis_to="")
Two chords sharing the vertex site.
.TP
.B TimingShift(name, seconds=None, turns=None, buckets_per_turn=None, rf_hz=None, rf_uncertainty_hz=None)
A fixed offset; \fBvalue_s\fR, \fBt_rev_s\fR, \fBrf_sensitivity_s_per_hz\fR.
.TP
.B Settings
Dataclass of run settings (clock_hz, earth_model, offset_normal, rounding, window, ...).
\fBSettings.from_dict\fR accepts the nested file layout (earth:, physics:, trigger_window:, sensitivity:).
.TP
.B Problem(settings, sites, baselines, timing_shifts)
\fBProblem.from_dict(d)\fR builds everything from a configuration mapping and resolves sites given
with \fBaxis_position\fR (along/right/up in the beam-axis frame) to geodetic coordinates;
\fBsite(id)\fR looks a site up.
.SS Engine (gps_tof.calc)
.TP
.B compute_all(problem) -> dict
JSON-serialisable result: settings, sites, one entry per baseline and one per opening angle.
.TP
.B compute_baseline(problem, baseline) -> dict
Keys: \fBsource\fR, \fBtarget\fR (site summaries with ECEF positions), \fBledger\fR (list of
correction steps with L_m, dL_m, dt_ns, dticks, cum_dticks), \fBresult\fR (L_m, t_s, t_us,
ticks, ticks_int, legacy_units), \fBgeometry\fR, \fBeffects\fR (sagnac_ns, neutrino delay,
cables), \fBtiming_shifts\fR, \fBtotal\fR, \fBwindow\fR, \fBsensitivities\fR, \fBerror_budget\fR.
.TP
.B compute_opening_angle(problem, opening_angle) -> dict
Keys: angle_rad/deg/mrad/dms, L_a_m, L_b_m, azimuth and elevation of each chord at the vertex,
delta_azimuth_deg, delta_elevation_deg, horizontal_component_mrad, vertical_component_mrad,
a_transverse_from_vb_m, b_transverse_from_va_m, a_along_vb_m, dL_m, dt_us, dticks,
path_via_a_minus_direct_m and, with axis_to, off_axis_a_mrad, off_axis_b_mrad, same_side_of_axis.
.TP
.B axis_frame(problem) -> dict | None
Origin ECEF \fBp0\fR, unit direction \fBu\fR, transverse unit vectors \fBh\fR (right, looking
downstream) and \fBv\fR (up), azimuth/elevation at the origin, length.
.TP
.B point_vs_axis(p, frame) -> dict
off_axis_mrad/deg, along_axis_m, transverse_m, transverse_right_m, transverse_up_m, clock_angle_deg, distance_from_origin_m.
.TP
.B direction_vs_axis(v, frame) -> dict
angle_mrad/deg between a chord direction and the axis, right_component_mrad, up_component_mrad.
Baseline results carry these under \fBbeam_axis\fR (chord_vs_axis, source, target); site summaries
under \fBvs_axis\fR; opening angles under \fBbeam_axis\fR (a_chord_vs_axis, b_chord_vs_axis, a, b, vertex).
.TP
.B compute_face(problem, site) -> dict
For a site with \fBface\fR: \fBpoints\fR (left, center, right, top, bottom with lat/lon/h, ECEF and
\fBvs_axis\fR), \fBsubtended_at_axis_origin_mrad\fR (left_right, top_bottom) and \fBopening_angles\fR
(per configured opening angle involving the site: the angle for each face point).  Included in
\fBcompute_all\fR as \fBfaces\fR; the derived edge sites appear in \fBProblem.sites\fR.
.TP
.B chord(a, b, settings, stage) -> float
Chord length between two sites for a given \fBStage\fR (which corrections are applied);
\fBfinal_stage(settings)\fR is the fully corrected stage, \fBsite_point(site, settings, stage)\fR the ECEF endpoint.
.SS Geodesy (gps_tof.geodesy)
\fBgeodetic_to_ecef(lat, lon, h, ell=WGS84)\fR, \fBecef_to_geodetic(p, ell)\fR,
\fBspherical_to_ecef(lat, lon, h, R)\fR, \fBenu_basis(lat, lon)\fR,
\fBenu_to_ecef_offset(d_enu, lat, lon, up="geodetic"|"radial", p=None)\fR,
\fBazimuth_elevation(v, lat, lon)\fR, vector helpers \fBnorm\fR, \fBdot\fR, \fBcross\fR,
\fBangle_between\fR.  Angles in radians.
.SS Fermilab site frame (gps_tof.fermilab_site, gps_tof.projection)
\fBfscs_to_geodetic(x_ft, y_ft, z_ft, geoid_n_m=-32.78456) -> (lat_deg, lon_deg, h_m)\fR,
\fBgeodetic_to_fscs(lat_deg, lon_deg, h_m)\fR, \fBfscs_bearing_to_azimuth(bearing_deg)\fR.
\fBObliqueStereographic(ell, lat0, lon0, k0, false_e, false_n)\fR with \fBforward\fR/\fBinverse\fR
implements EPSG method 9809.
.SS Report (gps_tof.report)
\fBrender(result, fmt)\fR with fmt in "text", "md", "json".
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
from gps_tof.model import Problem
from gps_tof.calc import compute_baseline
p = Problem.from_dict({"sites": [
      {"name": "ND", "lat": "41 50 23 N", "lon": "88 16 13 W", "height_m": 228, "offset_enu_m": [0, 0, -120]},
      {"name": "FD", "lat": "48 22.715780 N", "lon": "92 49.876930 W", "height_m": 348.638, "offset_enu_m": [0, 0, -19.8]}]})
r = compute_baseline(p, p.baselines[0])
print(r["result"]["L_m"], r["result"]["ticks"], [(s["step"], s["dticks"]) for s in r["ledger"]])
.fi
